# Writing Principles (local files)

Use markdown under `Writing Principles/` for writing craft: structure, voice, checklists, persuasion.

Hosted Writing MCP tools and `internal_knowledge_*` writing blocks are **retired**. Do not call `writing_get_*` tools.

## Routing

| Task | Load |
|------|------|
| Any structured writing | `Writing Principles/CORE_WRITING_PRINCIPLES.md` first |
| B2B / Rocket proposal | `PROPOSAL_WRITING_PRINCIPLES.md` + CRM Knowledge `search_docs` for product facts |
| Custom / government proposal | Core + `workflows/general-proposal/` scaffolds; **no** CRM product facts unless the bid needs them |
| Sales slides | `SALES_PRESENTATION_SLIDE_PRINCIPLES.md` |
| Catalog names / summaries | `SALES_FEATURE_COPY_PRINCIPLES.md` (after Core §6–8) |
| Pricing sheet / features summary | `CANONICAL_VIEW_COPY_PRINCIPLES.md` (after Core §6–8) |
| Sales agent consult (client-ready + briefing) | `SALES_AGENT_OUTPUT_PRINCIPLES.md` (after Core §1, §9) |
| Web copy | `WEB_PAGE_COPY_PRINCIPLES.md` |
| Feature guides | `FEATURE_GUIDE_WRITING_PRINCIPLES.md` |
| Localization | `TRANSLATION_PRINCIPLES.md` / `TRANSLATION_PHILOSOPHY.md` |

See `Writing Principles/INDEX.md` and `docs/WRITING_PRINCIPLES_MCP.md`.

**Truth boundary:** Writing Principles = how to write. CRM Knowledge MCP (`search_docs`) = what the product does.
